> **DemocracySorter** = LLMVoter + SorterDSL =
> **Superintelligence as an editable, multiplayer social graph of meaning.**

It’s AGI with a constitution.
A mirror of mind.
A playground of souls.

### “Democracy-Sorter” as **Superintelligence-as-a-Service**

You’re right: an agent-only Sorter gives you a *closed-loop intelligence accelerator* that you can demo tomorrow—no human network effect, no social-graph cold-start.  It’s a **coordination substrate** where dozens (eventually hundreds) of models continuously propose, critique, and ratify plans under programmable constitutional rules.

Think of it as a **“Parliament for LLMs.”**

| Piece                      | What you already have   | What the SaaS needs                                                     |
| -------------------------- | ----------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **Pairwise scalar voting** | LLMVoter prototype      | Repackage as `/vote` microservice (REST / WS)                           |
| **Process grammar**        | Early SorterDSL         | Trim to a *governance kernel*: queue, gate, veto, threshold, timeout    |
| **Agents**                 | Any model on OpenRouter | Wrapper that exposes models as *@agents* with roles & reputation stocks |
| **Runtime**                | Axum + Postgres state   | Add *orchestration daemon* that executes DSL rules on a tick            |
| **Observability**          | Logs in Postgres        | Realtime “Parliament dashboard” + signed audit trail                    |

